WEBVTT

00:03.740 --> 00:06.980
Zenos, I'm looking forward 
to buying some new tea!

00:06.980 --> 00:10.480
Yeah? Well, I'm looking 
forward to you making it.

00:32.450 --> 00:34.340
Hey. What are you doing?

00:35.750 --> 00:36.760
Nothing.

00:37.220 --> 00:40.930
Well, if you're not doing anything, 
how about adventuring with us?

00:42.790 --> 00:45.350
It's not like you've got 
anywhere else to be, right?

00:45.840 --> 00:48.560
I heard people from the slums 
couldn't become adventurers.

00:48.560 --> 00:50.320
Normally, yeah.

00:50.320 --> 00:53.000
But I think that if you're 
motivated and have the skills,

00:53.000 --> 00:55.820
then your status doesn't matter.

00:55.820 --> 00:58.030
Is there anything you can do?

00:58.030 --> 01:00.870
I know a bit of healing magic.

01:01.840 --> 01:04.040
Healing magic?

01:04.040 --> 01:06.790
Poor folks can't afford 
that kind of education.

01:06.790 --> 01:08.790
There's no way.

01:08.790 --> 01:11.380
Well, you can join our party.

01:11.380 --> 01:14.340
I don't expect you to contribute much.

01:14.340 --> 01:17.220
I just really want a slave.

01:38.800 --> 01:41.420
<i>These kinds of creatures are nothing to me.</i>

01:42.350 --> 01:44.120
<i>But, man...</i>

01:44.120 --> 01:48.420
<i>He really is useless. Like lugging 
a bunch of baggage around.</i>

01:50.840 --> 01:52.040
<i>It's about time...</i>

01:54.550 --> 01:56.490
We don't need you anymore.

03:29.890 --> 03:32.480
Why's this damn place so far out of the way?

03:32.480 --> 03:35.050
I know this is our chance to 
earn points with one of

03:35.050 --> 03:38.070
the seven great nobles, 
but it feels like a waste of energy.

03:39.260 --> 03:41.950
I'm still feeling the wine from last night...

03:41.950 --> 03:45.100
The sooner we wrap this up, the 
sooner we can get back to drinking.

03:45.100 --> 03:46.000
Sounds good.

03:46.000 --> 03:51.210
Did you see the way the bar maid's eyes lit up 
when we said we were the Golden Phoenix?

03:51.210 --> 03:55.330
Looks like slaying multiple magic beasts 
without taking so much as a scratch

03:55.330 --> 03:58.430
has made us big news, 
even all the way out in the sticks.

04:00.640 --> 04:02.140
There they are.

04:07.720 --> 04:11.730
Let's kill these things and get 
their hides to Lord Fennel!

04:13.980 --> 04:16.440
Guile, just to be safe, 
whip up some defensive magic!

04:16.720 --> 04:17.860
You got it!

04:18.480 --> 04:19.800
Come forth, force!

04:19.800 --> 04:25.360
Become an unyielding shield to repel all that 
would do harm, as the spirit of lofty aspiration!

04:25.620 --> 04:26.870
Encase!

04:29.660 --> 04:31.750
Your pitiful attacks aren't gonna...

04:33.920 --> 04:35.290
It burns!

04:35.290 --> 04:37.040
What the hell?!

04:39.670 --> 04:42.170
Andres, hurry up with the attack magic!

04:42.170 --> 04:46.010
I-I am! I hereby defy the laws of 
creation and shake the foundation of—

04:46.800 --> 04:50.310
<i>Useless fool! Maybe I oughta fire him, too!</i>

04:51.120 --> 04:54.440
Guile! Where's the damn defense magic?!

04:54.440 --> 04:57.940
I-I'm casting it! But it doesn't 
seem to be working well...

04:57.940 --> 05:00.400
Because you're hungover?! 
Are you kidding me?!

05:01.280 --> 05:04.030
<i>Damn it, they're all worthless!</i>

05:04.420 --> 05:07.280
No other choice. We're pulling out for now!

05:11.990 --> 05:15.870
How the hell were you struggling 
against magic beasts rated only B+?!

05:15.870 --> 05:18.740
You weren't doing much, either!

05:19.380 --> 05:21.150
Look, I'm just throwing it out there,

05:21.150 --> 05:25.010
but Zenos couldn't have actually been 
using healing magic on us, right?

05:25.010 --> 05:27.650
There's no way in hell.

05:27.650 --> 05:31.010
Still, maybe we should hire a healer...

05:31.010 --> 05:36.340
The real deal, and not some 
worthless peasant like Zenos.

05:41.130 --> 05:43.920
It took us ten days to get here.

05:43.920 --> 05:47.320
You said your name was Umin, right? 
You'd better make yourself useful.

05:47.760 --> 05:49.960
I wouldn't expect too much.

05:49.960 --> 05:52.060
I normally heal in the capital.

05:52.060 --> 05:54.950
I just happen to have an adventuring license.

05:55.700 --> 06:00.680
I'm curious as to why the Golden Phoenix, who 
are famous for coming out of battle unscathed,

06:00.680 --> 06:04.380
would need the support of a 
mid-ranked healer like myself.

06:04.800 --> 06:07.630
A lot's happened, all right?

06:07.630 --> 06:10.260
Hey, is Yuma gonna be okay?

06:10.260 --> 06:12.910
Your archer friend?

06:12.910 --> 06:17.180
He should survive, but I don't think 
he'll be adventuring ever again.

06:17.180 --> 06:22.090
That just proves he wasn't 
Golden Phoenix material.

06:22.090 --> 06:24.860
The loss of an archer 
won't make a difference.

06:24.860 --> 06:27.860
Guile defends, I attack,

06:27.860 --> 06:30.490
and Andres uses attack magic for the kill.

06:30.880 --> 06:37.620
Lord Fennel wants a scarf made of firefox 
fur for his daughter's birthday present.

06:37.620 --> 06:41.540
And I am not missing my chance to 
get in good with the upper crust!

06:45.610 --> 06:49.510
I'll cut 'em in two with my 
treasured sword, Hunber!

06:49.510 --> 06:50.720
What?!

06:50.720 --> 06:52.470
An ambush?

06:54.480 --> 06:56.160
Guile! Defenses!

07:07.940 --> 07:09.190
Mr. Andres!

07:09.190 --> 07:12.700
<i>Defensive magic is no reason 
to get careless, damn it!</i>

07:13.940 --> 07:18.250
<i>Why can't I hit them?! Why?!</i>

07:18.250 --> 07:21.920
<i>My body feels sluggish. But why—</i>

07:20.140 --> 07:21.210
Hey!

07:21.920 --> 07:25.000
Mr. Andres is going to be in real 
trouble without proper healing!

07:25.000 --> 07:28.510
<i>Why? Why?!</i>

07:25.890 --> 07:27.560
What's the call, Aston?!

07:27.560 --> 07:29.670
You can't be serious about continuing this!

07:28.510 --> 07:32.320
<i>Why?! Why isn't it working?!</i>

07:33.010 --> 07:34.700
Are you even trying?!

07:34.700 --> 07:37.060
The defensive magic was in effect!

07:37.060 --> 07:40.100
If it wasn't, he would've died on impact.

07:40.100 --> 07:42.690
Well, a fat lot of good it does 
if he still gets hurt so bad!

07:42.690 --> 07:45.190
You're a healer, so heal him already!

07:45.190 --> 07:49.570
I have to cast and enchant the spell 
based on the condition of injury!

07:49.570 --> 07:51.270
I've done what I can for now,

07:51.270 --> 07:54.820
but he needs to be taken to a hospital with 
specially prepared magic circles, and soon!

07:55.690 --> 07:58.660
We don't have time for that.
 Fix him right now.

07:58.660 --> 08:01.090
Do you even realize what you're asking?

08:01.090 --> 08:04.570
Even the upper echelon of healers couldn't 
restore him in this environment.

08:04.570 --> 08:09.130
The only ones capable of that are a select 
few elite healers, or maybe a Saint.

08:11.090 --> 08:14.800
<i>We've been taking damage 
ever since I kicked him out.</i>

08:15.480 --> 08:16.970
<i>But it can't be that...</i>

08:16.970 --> 08:21.320
Hey, could there be someone 
capable of this elite healing magic,

08:21.320 --> 08:23.520
but without a healing license?

08:23.520 --> 08:27.360
It's hard to imagine, but... do you 
have reason to believe there is?

08:27.360 --> 08:29.320
<i>What am I even saying?</i>

08:29.320 --> 08:32.560
<i>There's no way that peasant 
could've done all that.</i>

08:32.560 --> 08:33.860
<i>I'm overthinking it.</i>

08:33.860 --> 08:36.230
<i>He was just the party's slave.</i>

08:40.600 --> 08:43.830
<i>It seems I was a fool for 
placing my hopes in your group.</i>

08:43.830 --> 08:47.040
<i>Begone, and don't darken 
my doorstep ever again.</i>

08:47.540 --> 08:49.280
P-Please, just hang on!

08:49.280 --> 08:51.550
Let me speak to Lord Fennel directly!

08:51.870 --> 08:55.440
I'm afraid milady's birthday 
has already passed.

08:55.440 --> 08:58.050
What could you possibly say at this point?

08:58.050 --> 08:59.590
But—

08:58.670 --> 09:00.310
Sir Aston.

09:00.650 --> 09:06.070
Lord Fennel's disappointment is not rooted 
entirely in your failed hunting attempts.

09:06.070 --> 09:09.720
If you had judged the task impossible 
and reported it as such,

09:09.720 --> 09:13.150
he could've avoided the 
embarrassment of having nothing

09:13.150 --> 09:15.360
prepared for his daughter's birthday.

09:15.360 --> 09:20.030
<i>How am I supposed to say "no" when it's a 
chance to get in with a big-shot aristocrat?!</i>

09:20.030 --> 09:23.040
I-It's not like that! We had a traitor!

09:23.040 --> 09:24.760
That bastard Zenos got in our way!

09:24.760 --> 09:25.790
Zenos?

09:26.770 --> 09:31.650
<i>That's right. I never gave Zenos's name
to make sure no one found out</i>

09:31.650 --> 09:34.410
<i>that someone from the 
slums was in the party!</i>

09:34.410 --> 09:36.430
I-It's nothing, sir.

09:36.900 --> 09:40.050
Please, just give us another chance!

09:40.050 --> 09:43.690
<i>I can't believe I'm having to bow 
my head to a damned servant!</i>

09:44.680 --> 09:49.860
And what, pray tell, can a party with only 
half its members intact do to make amends?

09:49.860 --> 09:51.300
You don't have to worry about that!

09:51.300 --> 09:54.530
We'll be recruiting members 
to make up for the losses soon.

09:54.530 --> 09:57.400
Next time, we'll be sure to get the job done!

10:01.630 --> 10:04.650
Hey, are you sure you 
should've said all that?

10:04.650 --> 10:06.040
We don't have any leads yet.

10:06.040 --> 10:07.840
Don't worry about it.

10:07.840 --> 10:10.540
There was one other member 
of the party, remember?

10:10.540 --> 10:12.000
Our slave.

10:12.000 --> 10:13.170
You mean Zenos?

10:13.170 --> 10:15.400
He'll be desperate to get back with us.

10:15.400 --> 10:18.300
He'll be weeping with gratitude 
the moment I offer.

10:18.300 --> 10:20.180
That's a great idea, Aston!

10:20.180 --> 10:23.910
<i>I don't believe Zenos was 
keeping this party going.</i>

10:23.910 --> 10:25.390
<i>I refuse to believe it.</i>

10:25.390 --> 10:29.520
<i>But the fact is, everything was 
going smoothly with him around.</i>

10:29.520 --> 10:34.650
I'll use him like I did when we started out
and regain all the fame that we've lost.

10:34.650 --> 10:38.200
The phoenix will rise again!

10:38.200 --> 10:41.320
I'm coming to get you personally.

10:41.320 --> 10:43.990
Be grateful, Zenos.

10:46.040 --> 10:46.960
You doing anything?

10:46.960 --> 10:47.790
Not a thing.

10:47.790 --> 10:49.540
Come on, I'm not asking that much.

10:53.280 --> 10:57.260
Hey, I'm starting to think Zenos might've 
already died in a ditch somewhere.

10:57.260 --> 10:59.930
Nah, he might still be alive.

10:59.930 --> 11:03.260
I did give him that gold 
coin as severance pay.

11:03.260 --> 11:06.370
I could almost cry at the thought 
of how generous I was.

11:06.370 --> 11:09.350
The slums aren't exactly small, though.

11:09.350 --> 11:10.770
How do we find him?

11:10.770 --> 11:12.760
I've got the perfect idea for that.

11:12.760 --> 11:17.500
We hire the three demihuman 
bosses to help find him.

11:17.500 --> 11:19.110
Crooks like that are always

11:19.110 --> 11:21.660
on top of everything that 
goes on in the slums.

11:21.660 --> 11:24.910
That makes sense! Good idea, Aston.

11:26.690 --> 11:30.910
Boss, this human wants to hire us.

11:30.910 --> 11:32.920
A job?

11:32.920 --> 11:37.300
I'm kinda busy, y'know.
I was about to go see the doc.

11:37.300 --> 11:39.250
<i>Damn, she's fine.</i>

11:39.250 --> 11:43.760
<i>Wouldn't mind having her in my 
harem once I become an aristocrat.</i>

11:43.760 --> 11:49.470
I'm Aston, the leader of the Golden 
Phoenix, a gold-class adventuring party.

11:49.470 --> 11:52.100
That's an awful lot of qualifications.

11:52.100 --> 11:54.480
Sun's gonna set before you're 
done introducing yourself.

11:54.480 --> 11:56.290
Let's get down to business already.

11:57.500 --> 11:59.530
I want you to find someone for me.

11:59.530 --> 12:01.530
A man named Zenos.

12:01.530 --> 12:04.760
He would've made his way into 
the slums about two months ago.

12:08.630 --> 12:10.400
Oh, I see what this is!

12:10.400 --> 12:14.670
You're the idiots who kicked 
the doc out of your party!

12:14.670 --> 12:17.670
You certainly look dumb enough.

12:17.670 --> 12:18.590
Say what?!

12:20.570 --> 12:21.720
Run on home.

12:22.000 --> 12:27.080
The person you're looking for has better 
things to do than put up with your nonsense.

12:27.080 --> 12:29.850
And frankly, so do I.

12:29.850 --> 12:31.350
Who do you think you're talking to?!

12:33.370 --> 12:36.730
And do you realize who <i>you're</i> talking to?

12:37.760 --> 12:39.760
This is a waste of time!

12:40.610 --> 12:42.410
What was that, Aston?!

12:42.410 --> 12:44.110
How should I know?!

12:45.610 --> 12:50.240
Oh, so you're the party that was 
stupid enough to kick Sir Zenos out!

12:50.240 --> 12:54.250
Lynga thinks you'd be better off dying 
and reincarnating as toilet roaches.

12:55.690 --> 12:58.130
You know Zenos, too?

12:58.130 --> 13:00.980
Sir Zenos has no business 
with toilet roaches.

13:00.980 --> 13:02.960
If you know what's good for 
you, you'll run on home.

13:02.960 --> 13:04.260
Say what?!

13:04.260 --> 13:04.930
You wanna go?

13:06.300 --> 13:08.800
Lynga has no time for toilet roaches, either.

13:08.800 --> 13:09.860
Damn it!

13:10.430 --> 13:13.060
What is going on?!

13:15.960 --> 13:20.320
Oh? So you're the trash that kicked Zenos out?

13:20.320 --> 13:22.690
What business do you have 
with him after all this time?

13:25.020 --> 13:26.490
Wh-Who do you think—

13:26.490 --> 13:27.950
Stop talking, Guile.

13:29.030 --> 13:32.330
Hey. If I find out you've 
been harassing Zenos...

13:32.330 --> 13:35.080
We orcs won't take too kindly 
to that sort of thing.

13:36.510 --> 13:37.360
Aston...

13:37.360 --> 13:38.830
Not a word!

13:38.830 --> 13:42.800
<i>The three leaders of the demihuman 
gangs all love Zenos?</i>

13:42.800 --> 13:46.480
<i>That can't be right! It must be someone else!</i>

13:46.480 --> 13:48.930
<i>Some other guy named Zenos!</i>

13:48.930 --> 13:53.210
<i>There's no way that peasant 
has this kind of sway!</i>

13:53.210 --> 13:54.930
H-Hey, Aston...

13:58.460 --> 13:59.620
Zenos!

14:00.700 --> 14:02.320
This way, Lily.

14:02.570 --> 14:07.200
Wait up, Zenos! I'm still having 
trouble learning the streets.

14:07.200 --> 14:09.950
The slums can be kind of 
complicated in terms of layout.

14:09.950 --> 14:12.520
I'm surprised you know them so well.

14:12.520 --> 14:14.260
Is it because you used to live here?

14:14.260 --> 14:15.920
Hey! Zenos!

14:18.080 --> 14:21.740
Is that you, Aston? And Guile?

14:21.740 --> 14:23.590
You're damn right it is.

14:23.590 --> 14:26.840
Looks like you managed to 
survive somehow, Zenos.

14:27.220 --> 14:29.090
What brings you to the slums?

14:29.090 --> 14:32.470
Good question. Care to guess?

14:32.470 --> 14:34.560
Not really, no.

14:34.560 --> 14:36.600
Well, I'm kind of busy, so...

14:36.600 --> 14:39.390
G-Get back here!

14:39.390 --> 14:41.290
I came for <i>you</i>, damn it!

14:41.290 --> 14:42.230
What?

14:42.230 --> 14:44.370
I was looking for you!

14:44.370 --> 14:45.360
Why?

14:45.360 --> 14:49.700
Congratulations! I'm going to let 
you rejoin the Golden Phoenix!

14:49.700 --> 14:50.840
No, thanks.

14:49.970 --> 14:52.110
Don't go bawling in gratitude—

14:52.110 --> 14:53.910
Wait, what?!

14:53.910 --> 14:57.120
Did I hear that right?! 
Did you turn me down?!

14:57.430 --> 14:58.480
Yeah, I did.

14:58.480 --> 14:59.520
Why?!

14:59.520 --> 15:00.750
You even have to ask?

15:00.750 --> 15:05.000
Unreasonable treatment and next to no pay. 
There's basically nothing in it for me.

15:05.000 --> 15:06.250
Wouldn't most people say "no"?

15:06.250 --> 15:09.800
That's not what I mean! I'm offering 
you a chance to come back! Me!

15:10.510 --> 15:12.640
Look, if you're that desperate,

15:12.640 --> 15:17.020
I don't mind accompanying you on a 
quest when I have some free time.

15:17.020 --> 15:18.850
But you'll actually pay me this time, right?

15:18.850 --> 15:20.940
Huh? What are you even—

15:20.940 --> 15:23.100
50,000 wen for every healing.

15:23.390 --> 15:25.370
A million for critical injuries.

15:25.370 --> 15:28.610
Triple that cost if you need 
defensive and buff magic.

15:28.610 --> 15:30.030
Don't expect a discount.

15:30.030 --> 15:31.530
Who do you think you are?!

15:31.530 --> 15:34.280
It's not like you have a 
place around here, either!

15:35.100 --> 15:38.200
Dr. Zenos! How ya doing?

15:38.200 --> 15:40.400
Hey. How's your leg feeling?

15:40.400 --> 15:42.700
Pretty great, thanks to you!

15:42.700 --> 15:44.290
Glad to hear it.

15:44.290 --> 15:46.750
Zenos, come play with us!

15:46.750 --> 15:49.210
Who are those strangers?

15:49.210 --> 15:50.620
Hey, Doc!

15:50.620 --> 15:52.720
Appreciate you always patching me up.

15:53.020 --> 15:53.720
Hey!

15:53.720 --> 15:57.470
Zenos, these old guys are pretty noisy, huh?

15:57.470 --> 15:59.290
I am not old!

15:59.290 --> 16:01.100
Well, let's head on back.

16:01.520 --> 16:04.640
Are you serious about not coming back?!

16:04.640 --> 16:07.480
When it's <i>me</i> making the offer?!

16:07.480 --> 16:11.070
I was the one who took you in! 
Gave you a place to belong!

16:11.070 --> 16:12.270
It was all me!

16:12.270 --> 16:13.610
Sorry, Aston,

16:14.020 --> 16:15.490
but it's too late.

16:20.010 --> 16:21.370
Don't you ignore me.

16:22.690 --> 16:25.210
Get back here, Zeno—

16:26.380 --> 16:30.800
Bold of you to attack someone 
right in front of me.

16:30.800 --> 16:32.920
The royal knights can't overlook that.

16:33.370 --> 16:36.180
Huh? What brings you around, Krishna?

16:36.180 --> 16:37.800
I came to see you.

16:38.170 --> 16:40.140
But... I don't live around here.

16:41.040 --> 16:42.350
I got lost.

16:42.350 --> 16:46.960
That said, I managed to run into you, so my 
lack of direction has paid off this time.

16:46.960 --> 16:48.610
That's one way of looking at it.

16:50.480 --> 16:53.990
<i>She's supposed to be the youngest vice 
commander in the history of the royal knights...</i>

16:54.470 --> 16:57.870
<i>So why is she so friendly with Zenos?</i>

16:57.870 --> 17:00.990
<i>Just what are you?!</i>

17:01.370 --> 17:06.500
Now, I'm taking you to the nearest 
station for attempted assault.

17:06.870 --> 17:10.520
It's not like that! I didn't 
want to, but he forced me!

17:12.030 --> 17:14.970
<i>Don't you... Don't you ignore me,</i>

17:15.560 --> 17:17.040
<i>Zenos!</i>

17:19.540 --> 17:24.600
Come to think of it, the crew that kicked 
Doc out came calling on me the other day.

17:24.600 --> 17:26.480
They came to see Lynga, too.

17:26.480 --> 17:28.350
And they really did look stupid.

17:28.670 --> 17:32.690
I had an encounter with 
this trash party, as well.

17:32.990 --> 17:35.020
You three don't hold back, huh?

17:35.570 --> 17:40.020
I had a bad feeling, so I asked 
some of my boys to watch them,

17:40.020 --> 17:42.240
but they lost the trail.

17:42.240 --> 17:46.120
Same for Lynga. Even werewolves' 
noses have lost their scent.

17:46.120 --> 17:49.500
They've managed to stay out of 
the net cast by my orcs, as well.

17:50.000 --> 17:52.670
Maybe they just went home?

17:52.970 --> 17:57.560
That'd be great, but if they went digging 
even deeper, we might be in for trouble.

17:57.560 --> 17:59.080
Deeper?

17:59.080 --> 18:00.600
She means the underground guild.

18:00.930 --> 18:02.350
The underground guild?

18:02.650 --> 18:05.280
It's a guild that handles illegal tasks.

18:05.280 --> 18:08.910
The true bottom of the depths, which even 
our demihuman gangs don't trifle with.

18:08.910 --> 18:12.010
They'll do anything for the right price,

18:12.010 --> 18:13.610
which is why Lynga hates them.

18:13.920 --> 18:17.740
Drug deals, assassination, 
revenge by proxy...

18:19.070 --> 18:23.790
Then if those loud old men go to the 
underground guild and ask for something bad...

18:24.160 --> 18:27.500
You need a lot of money to hire people 
through the underground guild.

18:27.500 --> 18:31.920
Indeed. And if he bothered 
to seek you out, Zenos,

18:31.920 --> 18:35.460
I'd wager this fellow's 
finances are rather depleted.

18:35.460 --> 18:38.090
Which would mean he can't 
afford that kind of trouble.

18:38.490 --> 18:40.360
Th-That's a relief.

18:40.360 --> 18:42.220
Then we don't have to worry...

18:43.140 --> 18:44.730
Zophia?

18:44.730 --> 18:48.890
Well, I was remembering how 
I've been hearing about someone

18:48.890 --> 18:52.500
who will take jobs under certain 
conditions, even without pay.

18:52.500 --> 18:56.220
I think they called themselves... the Guide.

18:59.350 --> 19:00.800
Can't sleep?

19:01.870 --> 19:04.330
Lily? You're still awake?

19:04.330 --> 19:09.600
I was asleep. But when I woke up, 
I saw the lights were on...

19:09.600 --> 19:13.670
Want some tea? Or would that 
make it even harder to sleep?

19:14.220 --> 19:16.450
Actually, I would like some.

19:25.510 --> 19:26.850
How is it?

19:26.850 --> 19:29.500
As good as always. I appreciate it.

19:36.010 --> 19:36.910
What?

19:37.440 --> 19:42.820
When I can't sleep, you stroke my head. 
I'm returning the favor.

19:42.820 --> 19:46.700
Then I think I'll get a good 
night's sleep after all.

20:01.800 --> 20:04.000
Unable to sleep, Zenos?

20:04.000 --> 20:05.790
You're up, too?

20:05.790 --> 20:08.210
Well, there were three cups of tea prepared.

20:08.210 --> 20:09.810
How could I refuse?

20:10.350 --> 20:14.140
Has this run-in with your old 
party kept you from sleeping?

20:15.090 --> 20:17.780
What, you're worried about me?

20:17.780 --> 20:20.270
At the end of the day, you're 
actually pretty nice, Carmilla.

20:20.270 --> 20:21.820
Enough mockery!

20:21.820 --> 20:23.950
That's not the case, anyway!

20:23.950 --> 20:28.570
There's little to do at night, so I figured
I could go for a bit of conversation, that's all!

20:28.570 --> 20:29.830
Okay, sorry.

20:29.830 --> 20:32.800
This is too much tea for just me, 
so I'd appreciate you joining in.

20:32.800 --> 20:35.750
In that case, I see no 
reason to turn you down.

20:38.720 --> 20:41.840
I'd honestly forgotten 
about Aston and the others.

20:42.160 --> 20:46.780
But after being reminded like that, 
I kind of regret not slugging them.

20:47.870 --> 20:51.070
That said, I was actually 
thinking a bit further back.

20:51.760 --> 20:57.600
Zenos, you've said you learned healing 
magic while living in the slums.

20:57.600 --> 20:59.480
How is that possible?

20:59.890 --> 21:04.350
I was trying to revive a corpse, 
and it came with the territory.

21:04.350 --> 21:05.740
That's forbidden sorcery.

21:05.740 --> 21:09.880
Yeah. But when I was a kid, I didn't know 
anything about resurrection or the like.

21:09.880 --> 21:12.370
My teacher popped me on the head for it.

21:13.760 --> 21:17.130
You know, it's not exactly the same thing,

21:17.130 --> 21:20.310
but when I was among the living, 
there was such a thing as artificial life...

21:20.310 --> 21:22.210
The sorcery to create golems.

21:22.710 --> 21:24.590
Three hundred years ago, huh?

21:24.590 --> 21:28.090
That would've been during the Man-Fiend War, 
back when the Demon Lord was still around.

21:28.090 --> 21:32.160
It's a form of lost demon sorcery.

21:32.160 --> 21:33.850
They use a special kind 
of magic stone as a core,

21:33.850 --> 21:37.350
then add carbon and sulfur, among other 
ingredients, to create the golem.

21:38.050 --> 21:38.980
Huh.

21:38.980 --> 21:42.650
The way they felt no pain or fear

21:42.650 --> 21:47.430
and worked tirelessly on their 
tasks made them quite dreadful.

21:47.430 --> 21:52.040
What were you up to three 
hundred years ago, anyway?

21:52.040 --> 21:55.300
It was so long ago, I've forgotten.

21:55.300 --> 21:58.830
You really don't like to 
talk about yourself, huh?

21:58.830 --> 22:01.570
Well, I guess we should clean up...

22:02.670 --> 22:03.840
What was that?

22:04.150 --> 22:06.580
It came from the slums.

22:06.580 --> 22:07.720
Wait just a moment.

22:17.430 --> 22:19.350
Unbelievable...

22:19.840 --> 22:22.180
We were just talking about it,

22:22.180 --> 22:24.280
and now a golem is rampaging in the slums?

23:55.530 --> 24:00.000
The End of Adventure

23:57.150 --> 23:58.700
"The End of Adventure."
